 "id": "anti-windup",
 "needs": {
  "DataCable": 206,
  "MathBlock": 17,
  "WirelessTransmitter": 3
 },
 "newGame": false,
 "notesHtml": "<p><strong>Working principle.</strong> SCALE starts at 1. If the integral is below MIN and the error is still negative, or above MAX and the error is still positive, SCALE drops to 0 and the <a class=\"part\" href=\"/components/Accumulator\"><img src=\"data/icons/64/Accumulator.webp?v=3c4ea5c1\" alt=\"\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" loading=\"lazy\" /><span>Accumulator</span></a> stops taking input. MIN and MAX are not hard limits -- the integral can drift a little past them -- but this is good enough for most ships.</p>\n<p>The <a class=\"part\" href=\"/components/Accumulator\"><img src=\"data/icons/64/Accumulator.webp?v=3c4ea5c1\" alt=\"\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" loading=\"lazy\" /><span>Accumulator</span></a> must be in <strong>Pulse</strong> mode, clocked by the Reset_Clock channel, or it races.</p>\n<p>Tune the two thresholds and the I constant for your ship.</p>\n\n",
